// CreateLink: make a link.
//
// It is called at the Connection of the request's SandboxID, as [Client] says.
//
// A URL, for a browser or curl, into one thing of the sandbox: a terminal, the screen, a file
// to download or upload, or the browser for Playwright or Puppeteer ([BrowserLink]); or a
// private port's address and a token for it. It expires. A download or upload link works once.
// Making one wakes nothing.
//
// A private port answers only a request that sends its token as the header `Pethost-Token:
// <token>`: a program's, curl's, a page's fetch. The server checks it before anything wakes
// and takes the header off; the rest reaches the program as it was sent, Authorization and
// Cookie included. A preflight that names the header is answered 204 by the server itself, and
// the answer to a request whose token it took carries Access-Control-Allow-Origin with the
// request's origin, without credentials, so that a page of any origin may call the port with a
// token it holds. A browser's tab, a WebSocket or an image sends no such header: what a
// browser opens is a public port (Ingress), or a port forwarded by `ssh -L`. Every sandbox's
// address is under one domain: the server takes the Domain off a cookie an answer sets, and an
// app keeps the cookies its pages set to its own address with the `__Host-` prefix.
